{
  "_comment": "Authored mapping for design/bin/spec_figures_check.py. Each entry ties a figure printed in spec/target-spec.md section 2 to a column of a committed PVT record CSV. `row_match` (default `row`) is the prefix of the first cell of the one section 2 table row the figure lives in; all spec-text checks are scoped to that row. `reduce` is taken over the (optionally `where`-filtered) rows; `expected` is the printed worst case and must equal the first number in `printed[0]`; `tol` must be half a unit of its last printed digit; `at` is the binding corner and must appear (as e.g. `SS / −40 °C`) in some `printed` string. Each `printed` string must occur in the row exactly as often as it is listed, and every copy of the figure's number in the row must fall inside one of them. `at.supply_v` is the numeric binding supply (volts), required for matrix figures and compared with the selected CSV row via the matrix `supply_key`; the authored point must attain the extremum (any row tied with it qualifies). If a printed string renders the corner followed by a voltage (e.g. `FF / 125 °C / 1.98 V`) that voltage must equal `supply_v`; `print_supply: true` requires such a rendering. The checker only reports; it never edits the spec or any record. Each figure names a `matrix` in `matrices`: the authored, explicit expected PVT coverage of the (where-filtered) dataset it reads (axes + `supply` + `exclude`, or an exact `points` list). The checker rejects missing, duplicate and unexpected (corner, temp_c, supply) points and nonfinite values of the figure's key. Supply mode `paired_with_corner` records the existing methodology: VDD moves with the process corner (FF 1.98 V, SS 1.62 V, others 1.8 V); it is NOT an independent supply sweep. Smaller deliberate grids are written by narrowing axes or listing `exclude` entries. `campaign_figures` (offset Monte Carlo, issue #108) are read from a committed campaign summary JSON instead of a PVT CSV: see the checker docstring. `scope` (issue #186) is `current` or `historical` per entry: `current` requires the cited record's dut block to verify and equal design/netlist/opamp_core.spice; `historical` requires `historical_reason` and, for a record without a dut block, `legacy_unverified: true`. `scope_text` must occur in the cited table row within 600 characters before printed[0] (current: must say `current`; historical: must contain a historical word); a current figure's preceding prose may not use a historical word.",
